{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414811-about-enkidu","id":1414811,"title":"about Enkidu","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-20T14:17:54-07:00","id":1414811,"title":"about Enkidu","content":"I came across an old reddit post about Enkidu being the most physically powerful vampire alive. Which caught me of guard because to be honest, i really never thought about him. Enkidu is one of those methuselah's that went under my radar. But he has my attention now. I am going to quote the post below:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">''I don't really find anyone else, even other methusala of his age or much greater, that seems like they'd be able to compete with him without using a lot of sorcery. He has a 9 in both strength and Stamina, and his discipline and skill list is basically a selection of all the best ways to physically enhance himself even further past those limits.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Level 9 animalism: not just for controlling animals, this lets him do things such as enter and leave frenzy at will, enter a special controlled frenzy that gains you several different abilities from your beast, and as a neat offensive tactic, cause your enemy's own beast to attack them from within.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Level 8 Protean: Probably his most well known discipline, he uses it to assume various horrific forms for combat and hunting. In addition to the obvious ability to alter his physical form to increase his physical abilities even further past his base stats, he can also do stuff like automatically expel stakes from his body, transform into swarms of creatures rather than just one, turn to mist to avoid attacks, etc. Protean is an extremely versatile discipline, and level 8 is among the highest level we've ever seen on anyone. combining his natural tremendous power with skills like marble flesh would make him a walking tank.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Level 7 Potence, level 8 Fortitude: I combine these two because their effect is pretty simple: make him stronger and tougher. he's able to use advanced skills in both diciplines, and it's all being stacked atop his already huge base stats and the boosts he gets from altering his form with protean and frenzy. Basically, this guy can stack buffs like an MMO character.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Level 6 Vicissitude: This is one I think a lot of people probably glance over when thinking about Enkidu. he's actually reached the advanced level of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Tzimisce\" target=\"_blank\">Tzimisce</a>'s signature fleshcraft magic, in fact having a higher level in it than many actual <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Tzimisce\" target=\"_blank\">Tzimisce</a> fleshapers. This level is high enough to do thinks like assume the Zulo war form(possibly stack it with his other transformations?) as well as combine it with his extremly high Protean skill to have an ABSURDLY high level of customization to his body. Considering his advanced age and level of his disciplines, I'd imagine he could do some truly crazy things to his body.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Level 7 Celerity: Nothing fancy here, he's just very fast. combine this with his incredibly powerful body and he's pretty much just a blur if instant death.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">In addition, he has a 9 in the Body Alteration skill, implying he is extremely good at actually using all these disciplines on himself and could make full use of something like Vicissitude and protean.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Basically, Enkidu is a very specialized sort of dude, but he is ungodly good at this specialization. Most of his disciplines and skills work exceptional well together and can be stacked on each other in such a way as to pretty much just make him the ideal physical specimen for any given situation. taking his core stats and his skillsets into account, I honestly can't think of a single other vampire we know of who would be able to even match, much less exceed him, in terms of pure physical ability&quot;<br /> <br /> What do you guys think? Would you agree with this post? I think the guy makes a decent argument. Those stats are god like.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","user":"blackshade","date":". 09-20-2020, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T14:21:47-07:00","id":1414813,"title":"","content":"I think that was before Ur-Shulgi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T14:37:46-07:00","id":1414819,"title":"","content":"Ur-Shulgi without magic goes down hard to Enkidu, I think. Quietus nine is not nothing, but it doesn't stack up to Enkidus physical power.<br /> <br /> Although, Ur-Shulgis other disciplines are &quot;Not known&quot;. They could be quite significant and a match for Enkidu. Ur-Shulgi is about 2 000 years older after all. In the absence of other information, I'd say Enkidu dominates a purely physical fight, but we just don't know what the older Ur-Shulgi brings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T18:28:00-07:00","id":1414850,"title":"","content":"I'm going to have to go with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2471\" data-vbnamecard=\"2471\">Trollroot</a> with this one...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T19:20:56-07:00","id":1414861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414811-about-enkidu?p=1414819#post1414819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ur-Shulgi without magic goes down hard to Enkidu, I think. Quietus nine is not nothing, but it doesn't stack up to Enkidus physical power.<br /> <br /> Although, Ur-Shulgis other disciplines are &amp;quot;Not known&amp;quot;. They could be quite significant and a match for Enkidu. Ur-Shulgi is about 2 000 years older after all. In the absence of other information, I'd say Enkidu dominates a purely physical fight, but we just don't know what the older Ur-Shulgi brings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I alaways think Ur-Shulgi\u2019s most stats are at gens peak (aka. 8-9),and some of them may even exceed it, provided he is a badass of badass","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T23:47:40-07:00","id":1414878,"title":"","content":"IMHO, high end vampire fights are always decided by Auspex vs. stealth, followed by the ability of the attacker to deliver the overwhelming alpha strike. At lower generations especially, any attack that doesn't kill is wasted, as the defender regens it all with their dozens of BP per turn.<br /> Note that the attacker has the advantage, as they can blood buff in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T01:21:30-07:00","id":1414884,"title":"","content":"High end vampire will also use pawns in advance, the normal &quot;one versus one&quot; fight is very... street-level<br /> <br /> All stories involved killing a meth or more will be quite epic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T05:49:17-07:00","id":1414906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414811-about-enkidu?p=1414819#post1414819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ur-Shulgi without magic goes down hard to Enkidu, I think. Quietus nine is not nothing, but it doesn't stack up to Enkidus physical power.<br /> <br /> Although, Ur-Shulgis other disciplines are &quot;Not known&quot;. They could be quite significant and a match for Enkidu. Ur-Shulgi is about 2 000 years older after all. In the absence of other information, I'd say Enkidu dominates a purely physical fight, but we just don't know what the older Ur-Shulgi brings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would agree that Enkidu is the better combatant. However Ur-shulgi seems to be a plot device. He probably has some ass-pull powers that would allow him to make short work of Enkidu","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T14:04:16-07:00","id":1414965,"title":"","content":"For me actual builds always trump the cop-out vagueness of plot device, so my vote goes for Enkidu. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That said, it should also be taken in consideration that Enkidu's Protean &amp; Vicissitude combo affords an amazing variety of stealth options (along with its Obfuscate 5), as it might be capable of transforming in a variety of individuals - literally, considering it already has Swarm Form and might toy with funky variations out of it, like every beast in the swarm than turning into a different vampire. A coterie of one, instead of just Sabrina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-21-2020, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T16:23:13-07:00","id":1414985,"title":"","content":"Enkidu was written in a time in which disciplines levels justified the stuff writers wanted him to do. There was no depth into how Enkidu learned Vicissitude from the Tzimisce beyond that he had the power levels of the disciplines and that's it. The character was more of an idea for the ST to use rather than a story rich background to establish a chronicle on (beyond the fact that a 4th generation Gangrel from the Epic of Gilgamesh makes an extremely interesting background for a story).<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T19:49:18-07:00","id":1415009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414811-about-enkidu?p=1414985#post1414985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Enkidu was written in a time in which disciplines levels justified the stuff writers wanted him to do. There was no depth into how Enkidu learned Vicissitude from the Tzimisce beyond that he had the power levels of the disciplines and that's it. The character was more of an idea for the ST to use rather than a story rich background to establish a chronicle on (beyond the fact that a 4th generation Gangrel from the Epic of Gilgamesh makes an extremely interesting background for a story).<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Kind of. When you really look at what we are given of his story, he doesn't really sound like the mythic figure, more like a homonym.<br /> <br /> That said, there's a far from insignificant plot seed in his correlation of the Typhonian Beast's perenial corruption with the setites' continued existence, what could lead into some kind of &quot;bait to exterminate&quot; campaign against the whole clan. And he might be one of the few beings in WoD beside Kemintiri with a real chance of pulling it off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-21-2020, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}